# GBA per-port fstab (installed over /etc/fstab by etc/Makefile when
# MACHINE=gba). This is the SD variant, for the EverDrive (GBAED)
# kernel: its root filesystem lives on sd0b because the EverDrive's own
# FAT32 loader partition owns MBR slot "a" (sd0a) and swap is on sd0c
# (see sys/arch/gba/conf/GBAED). GBAED runs a real boot-time fsck, so
# this must name the actual root device.
#
# The plain GBA (mrams) kernel instead roots on the ROM memory disk
# mr0a and is read-only (romroot: it skips the boot fsck/mount). The
# top-level Makefile therefore swaps this file for distrib/gba/fstab.mrams
# (/dev/mr0a) in the ROM-embedded copy of the image only; the SD image
# keeps this sd0b version. There is no separate /home partition in
# either layout - /home is just a directory on the root filesystem.
# NOTE: lib/libc/gen/fstab.c's fstabscan() mis-parses a bare "#" or a
# fully blank line (it falls into the colon-separated "old style" path
# and returns EFTYPE / "Inappropriate file type or format"), so every
# comment line must have a space after '#' and there must be no blank
# lines at all.
/dev/sd0b	/	ufs	rw,async	1	1
